 all its successes and  perceived failings the ICC is still seen  by many as important and necessary just  as people in Afghanistan we know and we  are fully aware that it will not be  perfect  ivana son has been suffering for the  past 50 years and when people have never  had any chance of justice and  accountability and for that reason ICC  is the last resort it should be able to  break that vicious cycle of impunity in  Afghanistan and bring some sorts of  accountability to us  so are those US sanctions going to work  well the ICC says it will carry on doing  what it's doing which is sort of its job  to act independently and resist the most  powerful no matter who they are  if there's a news story you want us to  explain OnStar here get in touch with us  on Twitter or Facebook and make sure to  subscribe to al-jazeera on YouTube so  you're up to date with all of our  episodes I'll see you next week  you  [Music]

